                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>This inscription records the establishment of a temple for the local goddess (Bhaḻari) and its endowment by the Arasakka, the wife of Paḷḷigan who in turn was the son of Jōgayya and Nijabbe. 
                            This grant was made when Bhīmayya was ruling Banavāsi and Nāgārjuna was presiding over the administration of the region. Āhavamalladēva is identified here as <foreign>mahāmaṇḍalēśvara</foreign>.
                        </summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
